  Paragraph: The only world known to carry life. Liquid water covers about seventy-one per cent of the surface, the atmosphere holds the temperature steady, and a magnetic field turns aside the solar wind. Its unusually large Moon steadies the tilt of its axis and keeps the seasons regular.
